{"id": "EUVD-2026-103924", "enisaUuid": "4cf822ea-cc76-3248-9117-c68dec7b8d2b", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\niio: adc: xilinx-xadc: free IRQ before cancelling the unmask worker on unbind\n\nThe ZYNQ XADC alarm IRQ handler queues zynq_unmask_work via\nschedule_delayed_work(); that work is cleared by a devm callback.\nRegister the devm callback before devm_request_irq() so the devres LIFO\nteardown frees the IRQ first, ensuring the handler can no longer queue\nwork by the time the workqueue is cleared. Otherwise the handler could\nre-arm the work and run it after the xadc structure has been freed.\n\nThis issue was found by an in-house static analysis tool.", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:45:14", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:55:34", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/012451d72c12293918617ff98cc737bedad21910", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a29d385ad7b340c952a3935af2b33488db1eb3a6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a5fe2d1b55faba6d00fd87ad491b6cb603046304", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/49ea8a359e362bfbb32a647c8eb7962fbb37234e", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0f3f427076240e75ff265e61645627a71ca4918c"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-98670", "GHSA-pfxr-v75f-fxq3"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.17, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "25975a1d-667e-31e6-9cd1-c62d612db1fc", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.10"}, {"id": "286df2a2-de1d-3ea9-a6f2-df44e2c11a2a", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "2d0c4598-dc5a-3cdc-ba0d-98f2a04fd60c", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "33288ff1-f322-3eb6-87e5-bc2b47a96a92", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "55b754fe-a8d8-3ed1-886b-1f2864b6594d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "prod